ALVA — Launch Bounce / Wall Ricochet Combat Rework

Reference

Use this video as the visual/game-feel reference for the launch-and-bounce behavior:

https://youtu.be/C95FpcRLsbE?si=HoYArRHPnqhwB9rF

Study specifically the moments where a fighter is launched with significant knockback, collides with stage geometry, rebounds from that surface, travels toward another surface, and can potentially bounce again.

The target is the feel and readability of that interaction, not a copy of MultiVersus’s internal mechanics.

⸻

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Add a launch ricochet/bounce system to ALVA.

When a fighter is launched hard enough by an attack and collides with solid stage geometry, instead of the collision simply deleting their velocity, they should be able to rebound from that geometry.

Example:

Attack connects
→ fighter is launched horizontally
→ fighter hits a wall
→ fighter rebounds away from the wall
→ fighter flies across the arena
→ fighter hits another wall/floor/ceiling
→ fighter can rebound again if enough launch energy remains
→ eventually the launch loses enough energy that ordinary physics takes over.

The result should make powerful hits feel dynamic and should create situations where opponents can ricochet around enclosed or geometry-heavy stages.

This is specifically a combat launch behavior.

DO NOT make normal movement physics universally bouncy.

A character walking into a wall should still stop.

A character jumping into a ceiling normally should still bonk and stop vertically.

A character landing normally should still land.

Only sufficiently strong combat launch velocity should trigger ricochet behavior.

