⸻

FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The work is complete when all of these are true:

A fighter walking into a wall simply stops.

A fighter normally jumping into a ceiling simply bonks.

A weak combat launch does not automatically bounce.

A sufficiently strong combat launch hitting a solid wall rebounds.

A sufficiently strong downward launch can bounce from a floor.

A sufficiently strong upward launch can bounce from a ceiling.

Diagonal impacts preserve sensible tangential momentum.

A powerful fighter can bounce from one wall toward another.

Second and subsequent bounces are weaker.

The fighter eventually exits the ricochet state naturally.

Void behavior remains untouched.

Launch Point continues controlling overall knockback strength.

Shield continues working.

Dash continues working.

Charge continues working.

Shuriken continues working.

Clone continues working.

Sphere Rush continues working.

Existing abilities remain ALVA abilities.

Combos can capitalize on bounce trajectories.

The physics remains deterministic at ALVA’s fixed simulation rate.

And most importantly:

A strong launch into stage geometry should produce that satisfying “WHAM → rebound → fly across the stage → potentially hit another surface and bounce again” feeling shown in the reference video, without turning normal ALVA movement into pinball physics.
